rance\" title=\"Commons:Copyright rules by territory/France\">more information</a>), Russians who served in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink/Interwiki\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eastern%20Front%20(World%20War%20II)\" title=\"w:Eastern Front (World War II)\" class=\"extiw\">the Eastern Front of World War II</a> (known as the Great Patriotic War in Russia) and posthumously <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink/Interwiki\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rehabilitation%20(Soviet)\" title=\"w:Rehabilitation (Soviet)\" class=\"extiw\">rehabilitated</a> victims of Soviet repressions (<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Template:PD-Russia\" title=\"Template:PD-Russia\">more information</a>).</div><span class=\"mw-empty-elt\"><link rel=\"mw:PageProp/Category\" href=\"./Category:PD-old_missing_SDC_copyright_status\"></span></small></td></tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;font-size:x-small;line-height:140%;\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink/Interwiki\" href=\"https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/deed.en\" title=\"ccorg:publicdomain/mark/1.0/deed.en\" class=\"extiw\">This file has been identified as being free of known restrictions under copyright law, including all related and neighboring rights.</a></td></tr>\n</tbody></table><span class=\"licensetpl_link\" style=\"display:none;\">https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/</span><span class=\"licensetpl_short\" style=\"display:none;\">PDM</span><span class=\"licensetpl_long\" style=\"display:none;\">Creative Commons Public Domain Mark 1.0</span><span class=\"licensetpl_link_req\" style=\"display:none;\">false</span><span class=\"licensetpl_attr_req\" style=\"display:none;\">false</span><link rel=\"mw:PageProp/Category\" href=\"./Category:CC-PD-Mark\">\n<link rel=\"mw:PageProp/Category\" href=\"./Category:PD_Old\"><link rel=\"mw:PageProp/Category\" href=\"./Category:PD-old_missing_SDC_copyright_status\">"
